WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.067
-Donald Trump's son,
Don Jr., took the stand today

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.634
in the Manhattan
civil fraud trial

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.934
that could cost the Trump family
their entire business empire.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.968
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:15.200
♪♪

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.534
Donald Trump is facing
four separate criminal cases

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.267
and a civil fraud trial
in Manhattan,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.767
and so far, it's been
the civil fraud trial

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.334
that seems to have
triggered him the most.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.434
And that's because,
one, it's in New York,

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.367
and two,
his entire personal mythology

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:31.167
is built on his
supposed business acumen,

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.534
although at this point,

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.133
who still really thinks Trump
is a great businessman?

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:38.901
Do the houses of great
businessmen have cardboard boxes

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:41.634
stacked up
in fake marble bathrooms

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.434
next to curtain rods
from Bed Bath and Beyond?

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:48.634
"Oh, this must be the home
of Andrew Carnegie.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:49.667
What's that? It's not?

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.834
It's the home of a man

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:53.901
soon to be featured
on 'Hoarders Extreme'?

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.167
Color me gobsmacked."

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.834
If you used the bathroom
at your bank

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:01.901
and you walked in
and it looked like this,

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:06.033
you would know that your money
is already gone.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.300
And it's not just that picture.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.801
Remember this picture
from the breakfast buffet

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.267
at his golf club in Florida?

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.467
The one where Trump
is dressed as a Band-aid?

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.300
For some reason,
that doesn't look like

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.367
the golf club
of a wealthy businessman to me.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.300
That looks like
a retirement home

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.767
that's currently under
investigation by the state.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:24.934
And you can tell
this case in particular

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.133
has really spooked Trump,

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.434
because he can't stop
talking about it,

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:28.734
even at campaign rallies

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.033
where he's supposed to be
talking himself up,

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.200
not advertising all the bad
stuff that's happening to him.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.334
In fact,
if you were the average person

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.734
who doesn't follow
all the daily ins and outs

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.400
of Trump's civil fraud trial,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.167
how the hell can you
even follow any of this?

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.767
-I have a highly partisan judge,

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.634
a real political guy
right out of the clubhouses,

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:51.501
and he's been overturned many
times by the appellate courts,

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.167
and he defrauded me.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.901
They defrauded me,

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.968
because I have
a house that's very valuable,

00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:01.901
and they try and make it like
I'm increasing values.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:04.567
And honestly,
it's a very conservative number.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.300
But they valued a house
that's worth 100 times

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.467
more than the number they used,
let's say 50 to 100.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.634
They valued it at $18 million.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.167
And people say it's worth
anywhere from 50 to 100,

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.934
and maybe even that more.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.901
They defrauded me,

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:23.901
and he called me a fraud
before I even got to court.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:26.334
I said, "How the hell
can a guy do that?"

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.634
Called me a fraud
before I got to court.

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:40.634
-If you were in that crowd
for that Trump rally,

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:41.701
you got to be so bummed.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:42.934
That is not what you came for.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.701
That is never what you come for.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.033
You know, there's a guy in the
crowd holding a lighter yelling,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.701
"Do 'build the wall'!"

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.601
That's like
go to a Springsteen concert

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:53.868
to hear "Glory Days,"
and instead,

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:57.167
he complains about
property taxes for 45 minutes.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.667
"Hey, speaking of glory days,

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.367
remember when sales tax
was only 3%?

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.868
Now it's over 6%.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.567
I bought some deodorant
at CVS the other day.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:09.868
I said, $0.36?
$0.36 for sales tax.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:12.133
You got to be kidding me.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.834
Then I got to pay $20,000
a year in property taxes

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.334
just because I live
on Thunder Road.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:20.634
Two, three, four!"

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:24.067
Now if we translate that
to human English,

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.167
Trump is saying
the judge undervalued

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.534
his Mar-a-Lago estate,

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.834
and that some people
say it's worth anywhere

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.968
from 50 to 100 times more,
which makes no sense.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:35.033
There's not that much mystery
around the value of a home.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.200
Let's say you have a house.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.934
You paid $1 million
for it five years ago.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.434
I can tell you
what it's worth now --

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.200
a little more than a million.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.300
Mar-a-Lago is valued
at $18 million,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.434
and Trump said someone told him

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.300
it was worth
$100 million or more.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.067
Zillow that [bleep], dude.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.601
It's Palm Beach.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:52.634
You know it's not the only
tacky swamp castle in the area.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.100
Get some comps.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.701
Find another 18-bedroom hotel
and see what that's going for,

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:00.667
and what that is worth
is what yours is worth,

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.334
minus whatever
the buyer subtracts

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:05.634
because the bathrooms
are filled with boxes.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:09.133
But while Trump is claiming
his statements were accurate,

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.868
he also keeps insisting he can't
be held liable for fraud

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.634
because all of
his financial documents

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.434
have disclaimers
on them that say,

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.067
"don't believe any of this."

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.801
For real.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:22.601
That is an actual thing
he keeps saying.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:25.000
-We have
a clause in the contract.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.767
It's like
a "buyer beware" clause.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:31.501
It says when you take a look
at the financial statement,

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.100
don't believe anything you read.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.234
This is up front.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.400
"Don't believe
anything you read."

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.000
Some people call it
a worthless clause,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.667
because it makes the statement

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.634
and anything you read
in the statement worthless.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:45.067
It says, "Go out
and do your own research.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.868
Go out and do your own
due diligence."

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.267
You have to study
the statement carefully.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:51.567
Do not believe anything.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:52.701
You know what a disclaimer is?

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.567
You have a clause up front,
it says,

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.734
"Do not believe
these statements.

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:57.968
They were made by management.

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.601
They may be high,
they may be low,

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:02.434
they may be this,
but do your own due diligence.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.434
Do your own research.
Do everything.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.868
Do not believe
a word in them."

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.234
-Interesting.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:11.334
Is that disclaimer also on
the podium at your rallies?

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:14.767
I will say, it's not a bad
disclaimer for Trump to use.

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.367
I mean, I wouldn't be surprised

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.300
if that's how he ended
his wedding vows.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.868
"To have and to hold for as long
as we both may live.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.701
And also, those are just words.

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:25.100
Do your own research,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.400
because I've said it twice
before and I am single, so..."

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.234
Also, I'm sorry,
I didn't go to business school,

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.601
but I have a hard time believing

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.901
that actual financial documents
have disclaimers on them

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.634
that say, "do not believe
a word of what this says."

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:40.200
It would be like if your doctor
gave you a bottle of pills

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.534
and told you
to take three a day

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:42.968
and you said,
"Okay, what are they?"

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.000
And he said, "Oh, I don't know.
I found them on a bus."

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.400
We're talking about
the fundamental pillars

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.667
of our entire financial system.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.100
You have to be able to trust
what something is worth,

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.801
whether you're buying
real estate or equities

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.133
or bonds,
or hell, even if you're just

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:56.033
Bruce Springsteen
buying deodorant at CVS.

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.133
That's how our finan--

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:04.400
"Whoa, whoa, little Stevie,
did you see this?"

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.434
If that's the crux
of Trump's defense,

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.834
then I have to believe
his case is in bad shape.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.467
Some of what we've already
heard sounds pretty bad.

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:13.834
For example, years ago,

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.801
Trump expressed interest
in buying the Buffalo Bills,

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:19.033
but when it came time
to offer evidence of his assets

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.701
to back up
his ability to buy the team,

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.534
what he offered
was not convincing.

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:26.467
-So there's this former
Morgan Stanley executive who

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:30.033
testified today that back
when Trump was trying to buy

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:32.367
the Buffalo Bills football team,

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:38.667
he sent a letter claiming that
his net worth was $8 billion.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:41.400
And then in a meeting with
the Buffalo Bills management,

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.067
Trump handed out
a "Forbes" article

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:49.634
of the top-paid entertainers
to back up that claim.

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:53.267
Does this sort
of testimony bolster

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:56.234
what the prosecutors
are alleging?

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.601
-It does, Jake.

00:06:57.601 --> 00:07:00.334
Using a "Forbes" magazine
or any magazine article

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:03.300
to justify your net worth
does not cut it in a court case.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.133
-Be honest.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:07.467
If Donald Trump showed up
to your office with a magazine,

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:09.267
would you be worried
he was going to use it

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:13.434
as a financial document or that
he was intending to take a dump?

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:15.734
"You can't use a magazine
as proof of liquidity!

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:16.767
We're done here."

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:17.901
"You might be done here,

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:22.033
but I still have
some business to attend to.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:26.300
Now, could someone point me to
the classified document room?"

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.634
"I'm about to...

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.767
I'm about to clog up
a file cabinet."

00:07:37.167 --> 00:07:39.801
Also, thank God
Trump never bought the team.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:41.934
because the good people
of Buffalo have suffered enough.

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:43.467
It's one thing to lose
four Super Bowls.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:44.968
It'd be another
to have an owner

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:48.868
who claimed, actually,
we won four Super Bowls.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.400
Coach Giuliani giving
postgame press conferences

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.067
claiming,
"The kick wasn't wide right.

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:55.667
They moved the goalposts."

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:57.200
So the case is already
going badly for Trump,

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.501
but today
may well have gotten worse

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:01.300
because as of this taping,
his eldest son, Don Jr.,

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.267
was scheduled to take the stump.

00:08:03.267 --> 00:08:05.801
Sorry, take the stand.

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:08.834
What's interesting about this is
in a criminal case,

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:10.501
he wouldn't necessarily
have to testify,

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:12.100
but because
it's a civil trial,

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.100
prosecutors can subpoena him
and force him to comply,

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.567
and that's why he had
to show up in person.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:18.000
In fact, here he is arriving

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.968
at the Manhattan courthouse
today, stumpless.

00:08:19.968 --> 00:08:22.801
And moreover,
unlike a criminal case,

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.400
if he takes the fifth,
that can actually hurt him.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.367
-If this was a criminal case,

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:30.667
a prosecutor can never force
a defendant to testify,

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:32.901
but because this is a civil
case, the plaintiff here,

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:34.434
the New York State
Attorney General,

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:36.667
can issue a subpoena,
which is mandatory,

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:38.701
which requires a defendant --
in this case,

00:08:38.701 --> 00:08:39.834
Eric Trump's a defendant,

00:08:39.834 --> 00:08:42.033
Donald Trump Jr. is a defendant,
to testify.

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:43.701
Their only other option,
though, Jake,

00:08:43.701 --> 00:08:45.467
is they can take the fifth.

00:08:45.467 --> 00:08:46.767
They can invoke
the Fifth Amendment

00:08:46.767 --> 00:08:48.300
and refuse to testify,

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.033
but if they do that,
under New York State law,

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:52.834
the judge can consider
that against them.

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:54.167
The judge can essentially say,

00:08:54.167 --> 00:08:55.801
"I'm going to assume the worst

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:58.200
about what your testimony
would have done."

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.667
So there's risk
either way here.

00:08:59.667 --> 00:09:01.367
-There's no wriggling
your way out of this one.

00:09:01.367 --> 00:09:03.300
If you take the fifth, the judge
could assume the worst,

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.534
and if you answer
the questions honestly,

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:05.934
you can incriminate yourself.

00:09:05.934 --> 00:09:07.834
There's no third option
where you answer the questions,

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:09.868
lie, and hold up
a disclaimer that says,

00:09:09.868 --> 00:09:12.000
"Don't believe a word
I'm saying."

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.067
And if Don Jr.
refuses to provide full

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:15.901
and complete answers,
prosecutors also have

00:09:15.901 --> 00:09:17.300
another option
available to them.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.934
-If they're not
forthcoming in their testimony,

00:09:19.934 --> 00:09:21.767
you know, when you have
a witness on direct,

00:09:21.767 --> 00:09:23.601
you have to ask them
who, what, when,

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:25.834
where, why kinds of questions.

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.667
You can't lead them
to the answer that you want,

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.734
but if the witnesses
aren't forthcoming,

00:09:30.734 --> 00:09:32.601
then James can ask
for permission

00:09:32.601 --> 00:09:34.701
to treat them
as hostile witnesses.

00:09:34.701 --> 00:09:37.467
She will almost certainly
have to do that here,

00:09:37.467 --> 00:09:39.767
and she can ask them
more pointed questions,

00:09:39.767 --> 00:09:42.868
questions that really divulge

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:44.801
the information
she's interested in.

00:09:44.801 --> 00:09:46.534
"Isn't it true
that you were present

00:09:46.534 --> 00:09:48.033
when this
conversation occurred?"

00:09:48.033 --> 00:09:49.901
That sort of a thing.

00:09:49.901 --> 00:09:51.167
-And it doesn't help Don Jr.

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:53.434
that he already comes off
as a hostile witness.

00:09:53.434 --> 00:09:54.567
The man has no chill.

00:09:54.567 --> 00:09:56.167
I mean,
just look at the way he stands.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:59.033
He's got his chest puffed out
like a guy at a bar

00:09:59.033 --> 00:10:00.467
saying the words, "Step off."

00:10:00.467 --> 00:10:03.667
He looks like he just challenged
a much bigger guy to a fight,

00:10:03.667 --> 00:10:06.534
and now he's waiting for
his friends to hold him back.

00:10:06.534 --> 00:10:08.601
"You want to take this outside?
Let's go.

00:10:08.601 --> 00:10:12.200
[Quietly] Alright, come on,
guys. He said yes.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.567
Somebody grab me,
or I'm gonna need a Band-Aid,

00:10:15.567 --> 00:10:18.300
and I mean the big one."

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.634
And if Don Jr.'s deposition
from the investigation

00:10:20.634 --> 00:10:22.200
before the trial
is any indication,

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.000
it's safe to assume
he won't be willing

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.567
or able to answer
many questions.

00:10:25.567 --> 00:10:27.567
For example, at one point
in that deposition,

00:10:27.567 --> 00:10:29.167
he was asked about
something called

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:32.901
Generally Accepted Accounting
Principles or GAAP.

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:34.434
It's a standard
business practice

00:10:34.434 --> 00:10:36.434
he claims he learned
in Accounting 101.

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:39.033
So you would assume he could
at least explain the basics.

00:10:39.033 --> 00:10:41.267
Here is how that exchange went.

00:10:41.267 --> 00:10:45.100
-Do you have any familiarity
with an acronym GAAP?

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.234
GAAP?

00:10:47.234 --> 00:10:48.801
-Generally Accepted
Accounting Principles?

00:10:48.801 --> 00:10:50.067
Yes.
-Okay.

00:10:50.067 --> 00:10:52.701
How did you become familiar
with that acronym?

00:10:52.701 --> 00:10:55.067
-Probably in
Accounting 101 at Wharton.

00:10:55.067 --> 00:10:56.567
-Okay.

00:10:56.567 --> 00:10:58.000
What do they teach you about

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.968
Generally Accepted
Accounting Principles

00:11:00.968 --> 00:11:02.601
in Wharton?

00:11:02.601 --> 00:11:03.767
-Well, I'm not an accountant,

00:11:03.767 --> 00:11:06.067
but that they are
generally accepted.

00:11:07.934 --> 00:11:09.601
-[ Laughing ] Anything else?

00:11:09.601 --> 00:11:11.100
-That's pretty much
what I remember

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.200
from Accounting 101, so...

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.534
-[ Laughing ]

00:11:14.534 --> 00:11:17.834
-Have you told me everything
you know about GAAP?

00:11:17.834 --> 00:11:19.067
-Uh, basically.

00:11:19.067 --> 00:11:21.601
-Well, I do not think
they will be showing that

00:11:21.601 --> 00:11:25.200
in the Wharton Business School
orientation video.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.501
"You want to see one
of our graduates crushing it?"

00:11:29.501 --> 00:11:31.334
I love that
it's a sworn deposition

00:11:31.334 --> 00:11:34.033
and they're all just laughing
at how bad the answers are.

00:11:34.033 --> 00:11:35.868
"This is fun.
We're having fun, right?"

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:38.767
I'm not totally [bleep]?"

00:11:38.767 --> 00:11:42.234
Also, he's so confident when
he knows what GAAP stands for

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:43.634
that he doesn't even consider

00:11:43.634 --> 00:11:45.400
there's going to be
a follow-up.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:46.567
"What do you know about

00:11:46.567 --> 00:11:48.133
Generally Accepted
Accounting Principles?"

00:11:48.133 --> 00:11:49.501
"That they're
generally accepted.

00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:52.267
Is that all?
May I leave victorious?"

00:11:52.267 --> 00:11:54.534
"Do you know anything else?"

00:11:54.534 --> 00:11:56.400
"Uh...

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:02.601
It's generally accepted that
they make fantastic clothes."

00:12:02.601 --> 00:12:04.234
Trump is facing
four criminal cases

00:12:04.234 --> 00:12:05.901
that could theoretically
put him behind bars,

00:12:05.901 --> 00:12:08.300
but this is clearly the
one that has touched a nerve.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.067
It threatens
his financial empire

00:12:10.067 --> 00:12:11.200
and his personal mythology

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.501
as a supposedly
successful businessman.

00:12:13.501 --> 00:12:15.767
The only good news is that
he may come out of this trial

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:16.901
with a new slogan.

00:12:16.901 --> 00:12:18.367
Instead of
"Make American Great Again,"

00:12:18.367 --> 00:12:19.534
he could sell hats that say

00:12:19.534 --> 00:12:21.000
"Get Angry At Prosecutors --"

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.734
-GAAP?

00:12:27.167 --> 00:12:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:29.501 --> 00:12:32.400
[ Applause ]

00:12:40.634 --> 00:12:41.767
I stumbled, I didn't --

00:12:41.767 --> 00:12:42.934
I stumbled over it a little bit,

00:12:42.934 --> 00:12:45.067
but it still
wasn't going to work.

00:12:45.067 --> 00:12:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.033 --> 00:12:48.467
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:52.334
♪♪

00:12:52.334 --> 00:12:54.167
Hey, everybody, thanks
for watching "A Closer Look."

00:12:54.167 --> 00:12:56.133
And as a reminder,
my brother Josh and I

00:12:56.133 --> 00:12:58.000
have started a new podcast

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.634
called "Family Trips
with the Meyers Brothers."

00:13:00.634 --> 00:13:02.300
We hope you listen.
We hope you like it.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.300
See you soon.

